ty-7667169e-9de4-503b-b68f-ed58d102783f" :activity/first-step "step-2cd8a19e-1f39-5c47-b2a8-8e4d001f8902"]] "retractions" [[17592186193194 :question/problem "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}, X_{4}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}∼Po(θ)$ with unknown rate parameter $θ$. You're given the particular sample\n$x_{1} = 4, x_{2} = 2, x_{3} = 1, x_{4} = 2$.\nThe log-likelihood function of the sample is given by\n$l(θ) = aθ + b\\ln θ - \\ln c$.\n\nFind the value of $a + b + c$.\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a Poisson distribution is given by*\n$f(x) = \\frac{θ^{x}e^{- θ}}{x!}, x = 0, 1, 2, …$\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."]]}]